cix-autonombot (AutonomBot)
===========================

This repository is a fork of houimliraed/autonomous_ai_rbt
(https://github.com/houimliraed/autonomous_ai_rbt, Apache License 2.0), an
autonomous navigation robot stack built with ROS 2. All files are licensed
under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).

Upstream base: commit a73d1a1 (2025-08-15, "navigation fixes"), the tip of the
upstream repository at the time of the fork.

CIX Technology Group modifications (Copyright 2026 Cix Technology Group Co.,
Ltd) include:

- CIX P1 (CD8180, aarch64) board adaptation and board bring-up scripts
  (`scripts/run_sim.sh`, `scripts/env.sh`, `scripts/setup_ubuntu.sh`,
  desktop launchers).
- NPU vision integration: YOLO inference on the CIX NPU via the
  `cix_ros_noe_yolo` package from the CIX Robotics SDK (not vendored here),
  handing detections to `advanced_vision_navigator`; optional NPU hand-pose
  teleop via the SDK package `cix_ros_noe_handpose`.
- Localhost-only DDS network isolation for simulation
  (`setup_network_isolation()`), CPU-affinity tuning, and RViz/Gazebo
  performance guidance.
- Adaptation and startup documentation (`docs/`).

The upstream README, media, and simulation assets are inherited from upstream.

Third-party assets
------------------

- The simulation worlds `small_house.world` and `small_warehouse.world`, and
  the models under `src/autonombot_description/models/`
  (`aws_robomaker_residential_*`, `aws_robomaker_warehouse_*`), are derived
  from the AWS RoboMaker simulation worlds
  (https://github.com/aws-robotics/aws-robomaker-small-house-world and
  https://github.com/aws-robotics/aws-robomaker-small-warehouse-world),
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates.

- The YOLOv8 weights file `yolov8n.pt` is NOT distributed with this
  repository. Ultralytics YOLOv8 weights are licensed under AGPL-3.0
  (https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yolov8/); users download them
  separately (see README).

- Optional CPU Ultralytics YOLO (`ultralytics` / `torch` / `torchvision`) is
  not a default dependency of this repository. Those packages are listed only
  in `src/autonombot_vision/requirements-cpu-optional.txt`. Users who need
  the CPU path must `pip install` them themselves and accept Ultralytics'
  AGPL-3.0 terms. The supported default remains NPU inference via
  `cix_ros_noe_yolo`.
